{
 "_doc": "krew-window-tick's jobs: copy to $KREW_HOME/window-schedule.json (krew-install.py does, when it is absent). Each job: name, unit (a systemd --user unit), offset_min (minutes after the window opens) or before_close_min, needs_min (skip tonight if less window is left), after [jobs] (start once they have a final verdict), hold_on_failed, status_line (the job writes $KREW_HOME/job-status/<key>-<day>.json), legacy_timer (while that timer is enabled it owns the job), scope system, enabled. krew ships the reference install's whole off-hours chain on krew's unit names (the User 2026-10-10: a clean install runs what the reference box runs): day-close, the M&S nightly (report only until upgrades: true in ms.yaml), the improvement round (lessons, research, team eval, improve-file, outcomes), pack drift, the unit-registry refresh, the architect notes, the dream night and reflect, the morning brief and the Daily as the window's close. The Wall-side jobs (pose sync, the mouth drill) are Crissa's, and a dated one-off report has no unit. `enabled: false` turns one off. `watch` is the Daily's roll-call (unit+scope or file, every_min + grace_min); the ticker ignores it. `_reference_install` is the machine krew was built on, its schedule and its Daily `watch` roll-call verbatim (its _note/_why fields left out: history, not settings; its `house` name prefix written `ref`, its memory disk `{memory}`); the ticker never reads it. Copy a row into `jobs` only when that unit exists on your machine.",
 "jobs": [
  {
